.TH DEEPIN-SPEEDTEST 1 "November 2026" "deepin-speedtest 1.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
deepin-speedtest \- open, private internet speed test
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deepin-speedtest
.br
.B deepin-speedtest \-\-cli
[\fB\-\-list\-servers\fR] [\fB\-\-ndt7\-server\fR \fIHOST[:PORT]\fR | \fB\-\-librespeed\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-save\fR] [\fB\-\-accept\-mlab\-privacy\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B deepin-speedtest
measures latency, jitter, download and upload speed. Without arguments it opens
the desktop application. With \fB\-\-cli\fR it runs a test in the terminal.
.PP
Tests use the open ndt7 protocol against the public Measurement Lab (M-Lab)
servers, or against a self-hosted ndt7 or LibreSpeed server. M-Lab publishes
test results, including the client IP address, as open data. Deepin Speedtest sends no
telemetry and stores its history only in \fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/deepin-speedtest\fR.
.PP
All connections use TLS with certificate verification. Network measurements run
in a separate, sandboxed process. Deepin Speedtest refuses to run as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list\-servers
List nearby public servers.
.TP
.BI \-\-network " mlab|librespeed"
Public server network to use. The default is the one chosen in Options.
.TP
.B \-\-high\-speed
Tune the test for lines faster than 1 Gbit/s.
.TP
.BI \-\-ndt7\-server " HOST[:PORT]"
Test against a self-hosted ndt7 server (wss:// only).
.TP
.BI \-\-librespeed " URL"
Test against a self-hosted LibreSpeed server (https:// only).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the result as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-save
Do not add the result to the local history.
.TP
.B \-\-accept\-mlab\-privacy
Accept the M-Lab open-data notice without an interactive prompt.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/deepin-speedtest/settings.json
Settings and self-hosted servers.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/deepin-speedtest/history.sqlite3
Result history.
